#### d. **Force Module Implementation: Finding Closest Primary Planet for Efficient Pull Calculation**

A `computeNetGravitationalForce` utility for a spacecraft:

```cpp
/* Compute total gravitational pull from nearest large planet */
float3 computeNetGravitationalForce(const Spacecraft& s, const Body* planet, const BodyList& otherBodies)
{
    float3 minDist = std::numeric_limits<float3>::max();
    float3 totalForce = {0,0,0};
    for (const auto* b : otherBodies) {
        if (b == planet) continue; // skip itself
        float dist = glm::distance(s.position, b->position);
        if (dist < 1e6f) {   // check if close to any interesting body
            float3 force = b->applyGravitationalForceToTarget(s.position, b->position, b->mass / s.mass);
            if (glm::abs(glm::dot(force, s.velocity)) > 0.02f) {
                totalForce += force;
                minDist = dist;
            }
        }
    }
    return totalForce; // simple aggregate for demo, in real code vector accumulation
}
```
Or, more accurately, accumulate all net forces by weighted sum from each body.

